{"title":"2017 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Joy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> thin rods, one each of every integer length from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78ed721adc9a4cb545c4949f7b24fcc62ad98a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665d4ca6471d70415a61cbec47f7886c3abaa582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. She places the rods with lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c9cc980f0d47c1d95d6dc57372f375410c0ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/9610aefefe393225dc6aa67ebd1184cb0796ba39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\text{ cm}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098f1d4ead503bd95b33474d00a69ec3052d8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> on a table. She then wants to choose a fourth rod that she can put with these three to form a quadrilateral with positive area. How many of the remaining rods can she choose as the fourth rod?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d1b55c0b487630b326d59375f9dc45f03fc6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 17 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 18 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 19  \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The quadrilateral cannot be a straight line. Thus, the fourth side must be longer than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df0ad62d177e42a99a0e697e5f64f102ed5cd430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - (3 + 7) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> and shorter than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a47ab8a5e4cf424eba1b9b437350de4d79dd8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + 3 + 7 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. This means Joy can use the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible integer rod lengths that fall into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93d84871b0a3d11e3bfa6cac25df7ac7edc0b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[6, 24]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />. However, she has already used the rods of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb31c48611ee89ca67a3b48cd02708e48c0999de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 - 2 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Vi1100kO9o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Vi1100kO9o</a>\n</p><p>~Math4All999\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href